Replace the captureAvailable delay arithmetic with a swappable pacing policy, and
add the three comparison arms for RQ3.

Base commit: 860464b, plus the deadline-ownership change committed alongside this patch

  NO_PACING    NoPacingDelayPolicy            - zero delay, same admission path
  OURS         DeadlineDeficitDelayPolicy     - the deployed budget/backlog deficit
  THERMAL_LUT  ThermalHeadroomLutDelayPolicy  - open-loop on ADPF thermal headroom
  CODEL        ControlledDelayPacingPolicy    - RFC 8289 on measured queue wait

Switch arms by changing CaptureAvailableDelayPolicyFactory.ACTIVE_POLICY, and
clear the metrics database between arms.

Device build:
  CaptureAvailableDelayPolicy.kt          new  interface + NO_PACING + OURS
  ThermalHeadroomLutDelayPolicy.kt        new  baseline 1
  ControlledDelayPacingPolicy.kt          new  baseline 2
  CaptureAvailableDelayPolicyFactory.kt   new  the one-constant switch
  CaptureAvailablePacer.kt                     delegates the delay, feeds policy hooks
  CaptureAvailablePacingSession.kt             takes the draft-start uptime from the pacer
  DeviceStateReader.kt                         publishes the last valid thermal headroom
  CaptureMetricsExcelExporter.kt               pacingPolicy column on the RQ3 sheets
  external/.../CaptureAvailableApmPolicy.java  log wording
  external/.../SavingDraftImageTaskManager.java  builds the pacer from the factory

Analysis only, not part of the device build - drop these hunks when porting:
  data/lut_calibration.py                 new  cost-matched Thermal LUT calibration
  data/rq3_aggregate.py                        four arms; skips uncollected ones

OURS is unchanged arithmetic: it calls the same compute*DeficitMs functions on the
same inputs, and every policy still reports the pacer's own
backlog clock so that column stays comparable across arms.

